WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.400
- How's it going?

00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:02.301
- Going good.

00:00:02.301 --> 00:00:03.468
- It's decent.

00:00:08.120 --> 00:00:09.531
- Is that it?

00:00:09.531 --> 00:00:10.701
- So, I grew up in Russia.

00:00:10.701 --> 00:00:12.320
I lived there from ages three to 15.

00:00:12.320 --> 00:00:13.651
Ever since we moved to the US,

00:00:13.651 --> 00:00:15.240
I've always been confused
by this question,

00:00:15.240 --> 00:00:16.131
how's it going?

00:00:16.131 --> 00:00:18.371
Like, no one ever answers the question.

00:00:18.371 --> 00:00:19.632
All right, I'm going to prove it to you.

00:00:19.632 --> 00:00:21.277
How's it going?

00:00:21.277 --> 00:00:22.110
Nothing.

00:00:22.110 --> 00:00:23.365
How's it going?

00:00:23.365 --> 00:00:24.198
- What's up?

00:00:24.198 --> 00:00:25.628
- Not even a little detail.

00:00:25.628 --> 00:00:26.878
How's it going?

00:00:27.885 --> 00:00:29.571
How's it going?

00:00:29.571 --> 00:00:30.771
Again, nothing.

00:00:30.771 --> 00:00:32.531
How's it going?

00:00:32.531 --> 00:00:33.448
I got this.

00:00:34.355 --> 00:00:35.424
What does that mean?

00:00:35.424 --> 00:00:36.257
How's it going?

00:00:36.257 --> 00:00:37.090
- How's it going?

00:00:37.090 --> 00:00:41.757
- He answered my, how's it
going, with a how's it going.

00:00:44.105 --> 00:00:45.458
So now that I've proved to you that

00:00:45.458 --> 00:00:47.367
nobody ever answers the question,

00:00:47.367 --> 00:00:49.172
how's it going, I'm going
to actually take some time

00:00:49.172 --> 00:00:50.141
to sit down next to someone and

00:00:50.141 --> 00:00:54.269
see if we can have a genuine conversation.

00:00:54.269 --> 00:00:55.259
- How's it going, man?

00:00:55.259 --> 00:00:56.342
- How you doing?

00:00:56.342 --> 00:00:58.453
- Good, dude. Busy.

00:00:58.453 --> 00:01:02.203
Yeah, it's been cra, I
mean, it's been crazy.

00:01:05.242 --> 00:01:06.474
- How's it going?

00:01:06.474 --> 00:01:07.307
Good?

00:01:07.307 --> 00:01:08.140
- Yeah, good thanks.

00:01:08.140 --> 00:01:08.973
- Cool.

00:01:08.973 --> 00:01:09.806
- Aw, this is my--

00:01:09.806 --> 00:01:10.639
- Nice to meet you.

00:01:10.639 --> 00:01:11.472
- Hi.

00:01:11.472 --> 00:01:12.305
How's it going?

00:01:12.305 --> 00:01:13.138
- Hey.

00:01:13.138 --> 00:01:13.971
- How's your day?

00:01:13.971 --> 00:01:14.804
- Nice to meet you.

00:01:14.804 --> 00:01:15.637
- Good?

00:01:15.637 --> 00:01:16.593
- Good.

00:01:16.593 --> 00:01:17.426
- Yeah, I give up.

00:01:17.426 --> 00:01:19.834
That was the most awkward
thing I've ever experienced.

00:01:19.834 --> 00:01:21.038
I thought it was going to be a video

00:01:21.038 --> 00:01:23.175
where I like, met all these people.

00:01:23.175 --> 00:01:24.358
No, it's extremely uncomfortable.

00:01:24.358 --> 00:01:25.191
It's awkward.

00:01:25.191 --> 00:01:26.489
No one wants to talk about their day

00:01:26.489 --> 00:01:27.768
or like, open up their feelings.

00:01:27.768 --> 00:01:29.015
So instead of putting myself through more

00:01:29.015 --> 00:01:30.608
awkward interactions,
I'm going to go around

00:01:30.608 --> 00:01:31.441
with a microphone.

00:01:31.441 --> 00:01:32.889
I'm going to see why people think no one

00:01:32.889 --> 00:01:35.972
answers the question, how's it going.

00:01:37.067 --> 00:01:41.289
(cheerful electronic music)

00:01:41.289 --> 00:01:42.769
- Sarah, do you have
time for an interview?

00:01:42.769 --> 00:01:43.602
- I--

00:01:43.602 --> 00:01:44.723
- Too late, we're gonna do it, so.

00:01:44.723 --> 00:01:45.867
- It's a one question interview.

00:01:45.867 --> 00:01:46.700
How's it going?

00:01:46.700 --> 00:01:47.533
- It's going good.

00:01:47.533 --> 00:01:49.283
- Eh, it's all right.

00:01:50.697 --> 00:01:53.031
How's it going with you?

00:01:53.031 --> 00:01:54.372
- It's good.

00:01:54.372 --> 00:01:55.205
- Good.

00:01:55.205 --> 00:01:56.388
- So how many times have you heard

00:01:56.388 --> 00:01:58.121
how's it going in the past week?

00:01:58.121 --> 00:01:58.954
- Everyday.

00:01:58.954 --> 00:01:59.972
How many times have you answered it

00:01:59.972 --> 00:02:00.988
other than saying it's fine?

00:02:00.988 --> 00:02:02.142
- Never. (laughing)

00:02:02.142 --> 00:02:03.988
- Why do you think no one ever answers

00:02:03.988 --> 00:02:05.041
the question, how's it going?

00:02:05.041 --> 00:02:05.982
- I just had this problem.

00:02:05.982 --> 00:02:07.948
I was in LA and everybody
was answering me.

00:02:07.948 --> 00:02:09.561
- You don't want to get
too personal I guess.

00:02:09.561 --> 00:02:12.871
- I think it's because usually
the answer is too depressing.

00:02:12.871 --> 00:02:14.388
I mean, go to a therapist.

00:02:14.388 --> 00:02:16.231
- Nobody's ever going
to say it's going bad.

00:02:16.231 --> 00:02:20.132
- I once tried changing how
are you to are you good?

00:02:20.132 --> 00:02:22.208
And everyone was like, do I look okay?

00:02:22.208 --> 00:02:23.147
Is there something wrong?

00:02:23.147 --> 00:02:25.175
- I hate when people,
like if people were to

00:02:25.175 --> 00:02:26.798
really ask me that because it would like,

00:02:26.798 --> 00:02:28.627
uncork some deep shit.

00:02:28.627 --> 00:02:29.576
- I never ask.

00:02:29.576 --> 00:02:30.958
- Oh, you never ask?

00:02:30.958 --> 00:02:32.488
- I just give like the head
nod and if you give it back,

00:02:32.488 --> 00:02:34.307
then I know you're good.

00:02:34.307 --> 00:02:36.536
- I honestly think the
world would be better

00:02:36.536 --> 00:02:38.758
if we just didn't talk to people at all.

00:02:38.758 --> 00:02:40.214
- What I'm realizing is that everyone

00:02:40.214 --> 00:02:42.368
at Buzzfeed hates interaction

00:02:42.368 --> 00:02:44.627
and is bitter and I'm
the only one who cares

00:02:44.627 --> 00:02:46.718
about connecting with other human beings.

00:02:46.718 --> 00:02:49.358
- I guess I could get rid of
how's it going completely.

00:02:49.358 --> 00:02:50.536
- My problem with how's it going

00:02:50.536 --> 00:02:53.667
is when people ask and
immediately stop listening.

00:02:53.667 --> 00:02:55.427
- So how was your day?

00:02:55.427 --> 00:02:56.260
- It's good.

00:02:56.260 --> 00:02:57.093
- Ding!

00:02:57.093 --> 00:02:58.536
(laughing)

00:02:58.536 --> 00:03:00.078
- So I'm currently editing this video

00:03:00.078 --> 00:03:01.856
and I just watched back all the footage.

00:03:01.856 --> 00:03:03.608
Even though this video is silly and funny

00:03:03.608 --> 00:03:04.707
and it's not supposed to be serious,

00:03:04.707 --> 00:03:05.928
I feel like there's actually a pretty

00:03:05.928 --> 00:03:07.896
important lesson to be
learned from this video.

00:03:07.896 --> 00:03:10.016
I think there's something
so important about

00:03:10.016 --> 00:03:12.328
listening and talking
to the people around you

00:03:12.328 --> 00:03:15.307
because you never know
who needs to be talked to

00:03:15.307 --> 00:03:17.304
or who wants to be heard
or who has some problems

00:03:17.304 --> 00:03:19.288
that they need to share,
so it's really important

00:03:19.288 --> 00:03:22.507
to listen and you should take the time to

00:03:22.507 --> 00:03:24.387
sit down and talk to the
people you care about

00:03:24.387 --> 00:03:26.896
and really ask people how's it going.

00:03:26.896 --> 00:03:28.124
So if you guys feel like it,

00:03:28.124 --> 00:03:32.374
in the comments below, just
tell me how it's going.

